  "name": "ci: release-to-npm workflow + harden main/PR CI",
  "slug": "ci-release-to-npm-workflow-harden-main-pr-ci",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "Set up a GitHub Actions release workflow that publishes to npm on a tagged release, and harden the main/PR CI workflow to production standard.",
    "details_md": "Two parts. (1) Release: a workflow (tag push or manual dispatch) that runs the gates, builds, and publishes the package to npm (NPM_TOKEN secret, prepublishOnly runs, provenance if feasible), with a clear version-bump/tag convention. Since v0 ships source (dist removed from npm files by the packaging fix), publish is a straight npm/bun publish. (2) Harden the existing .github/workflows/ci.yml: confirm it runs on PRs AND main, gates merges, has sensible caching + concurrency cancellation, and covers lint/format/typecheck/test/build/smoke (incl. the new packaging test). Depends on the slopworks->slopwork rename landing first (the release must publish the final package name).",
    "acceptance": [
      "A release workflow publishes the package to npm on a tagged release (or manual dispatch), using a repo NPM_TOKEN secret and running the full gate + build first; dry-run verified",
      "A documented release procedure: how to bump the version and cut a release",
      "The CI workflow runs on pull_request and push-to-main, gating merges, with lint+format+typecheck+test+build+smoke green, plus caching and concurrency-cancel",
      "The published package name matches the post-rename name (slopwork)"
    ],
    "context": [
      ".github/workflows/ci.yml (existing CI to harden)",
      "package.json (prepublishOnly, files, bin — set by the packaging fix)",
      "depends on the slopworks->slopwork rename",
      "follow-on to ticket_01KY93E2NTZ7WK156HEQRVKCN1 (packaging/distribution)"
    ],
